# npl-ref - reference-page UX direction for the three display states.
# Authored by the tag nitpick lane, 2026-10-14. Not yet generated.
schema: "0.4"
id: npl-ref-reference-ux
type: image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    Design board for a reference-documentation page, dark theme (deep
    navy-charcoal surfaces, near-white text, muted slate secondary text,
    a single indigo-blue accent). The page documents a reflection element:
    a post-hoc record a system writes after finishing a turn, split into
    named sections - what held, what to change, how it was checked, the
    measured result, and training follow-ups. The board shows FOUR stacked
    example sections, one per display state, each with a small uppercase
    caption above it. No marketing chrome, no navigation, no browser
    window - four quiet document panels on a flat dark page.

    Every panel is the same card: a faint surface fill, a hairline border,
    a 12px radius, generous but regular padding. Section captions inside
    the cards are small, uppercase, widely letter-spaced, muted. Body
    sentences are a clean neutral sans at full brightness. Hairline rules
    divide the sections. Everything reads as quiet instrumentation inside
    a spec document - a record, never a scoreboard.

    Section 1 - "FULL (LABELLED SECTIONS)": five captioned blocks in
    order, captions exactly ASSESSMENT, IMPROVEMENTS, VALIDATION, EVAL,
    FINE-TUNE. Under each caption one plain sentence at full brightness
    ("the approach held; one gap in the eval loop", "add a regression
    harness before the next run", "checked against three traces",
    "quality 0.82 vs 0.71 baseline", "retrain on the two rejected
    traces"). A hairline rule sits between consecutive blocks. Every one
    of the five captions MUST be present and every sentence fully
    legible - a merged paragraph with no captions is a failure.

    Section 2 - "COMPACT (LEDGER LINES)": the same five entries collapsed
    into five flat single lines with no section captions and no boxes.
    Each line leads with one small glyph marker (a small balance-plate
    glyph for Assessment, small sparkles for Improvements, a small check
    mark for Validation, a small straightedge for Eval, a small target for
    Fine-tune), then the section name in semibold, an em dash, and the
    same sentence from section 1. Exactly five lines, evenly spaced -
    four or six lines is a failure, and no line may wrap into a captioned
    sub-block.

    Section 3 - "CLASS-FORM SUBSET": identical card styling to section 1
    but only three captioned blocks - ASSESSMENT, IMPROVEMENTS, EVAL -
    each with its sentence and the same hairline dividers. The subset
    renders as a complete, comfortable card: no empty placeholders where
    the other two sections would be, no greyed ghost rows, no "n/a"
    filler. It MUST read as intentionally three sections.

    Section 4 - "SOURCE VS RENDER (SPLIT)": one wider panel split into
    two halves. The left half shows the raw authored record as escaped
    code text in a monospace font at reduced brightness: angle-bracket
    lines naming the element and its five child sections. The right half
    shows the rendered card from section 1. The two halves sit side by
    side under one shared pill row reading SIDE BY SIDE, SOURCE, RENDER
    with the first pill active. The code text is intentionally plain -
    flat monospace lines, no syntax highlighting colours beyond one muted
    tone.

    Typography: small-caps muted captions; neutral sans body; monospace
    for the source pane and the pill row. Hairline borders, small radii,
    spacing tight and regular. The element is a record of a finished
    turn - it never judges: no score badges, no progress meters, no
    pass/fail stamps, no occlusion - text is never hidden, dimmed to
    illegibility, blurred, or struck through anywhere on the board
    (concealment belongs to other elements, never this one).
  negative: |
    Light theme; white background; glossy gradients; neon cyberpunk glow;
    dashboard card grids; donut, pie, gauge, radar, sparkline or bar
    charts; progress bars; star ratings; score badges; pass/fail or
    verdict stamps; checkmark-vs-cross scoring; mascots; logos;
    watermarks; navigation bars; browser chrome; blurred, blacked-out,
    struck-through or illegible text; collapsed paragraphs with no
    section captions; ghost or placeholder rows in the class-form subset;
    raw class attributes or code syntax shown inside a rendered panel;
    more or fewer than the named sections in the full state; modal
    dialogs or toast popups; any imagery other than the four panels.
  style: |
    Flat minimal dark technical documentation, minimal-tech aesthetic,
    ledger-first restraint, hairline rules, small-caps labelling,
    WCAG AA contrast on every sentence including the muted captions.
attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-ref/npl-ref-enhanced-full-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-ref/npl-ref-enhanced-compact-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-ref/npl-ref-enhanced-class-form-1280.png
    role: reference
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-ref/npl-ref-primary-source-1280.png
    role: reference
output:
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
  formats:
    - format: png
      filename: npl-ref-reference-ux.png
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    state-coverage:
      weight: 0.3
      description: Exactly four captioned panels in order - full (five labelled sections), compact (five ledger lines), class-form subset (three labelled sections), source-vs-render split; each carries its uppercase caption.
      fail_signals:
        - "only one or two panels visible"
        - "panels unlabelled or mislabelled"
        - "full panel missing any of its five captions"
    record-not-verdict:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Every sentence stays at full brightness and fully legible; the element never judges - no badges, meters, grades, stamps, or occlusion anywhere.
      fail_signals:
        - "any sentence dimmed, blurred, struck through or hidden"
        - "score badge, grade stamp or pass/fail marker present"
        - "progress meter or rating stars present"
    section-anatomy:
      weight: 0.25
      description: Full and class-form panels use small-caps muted captions, hairline dividers, neutral sans body; compact panel is exactly five flat glyph-led lines with no captions or boxes; class-form has exactly three sections and no placeholder rows.
      fail_signals:
        - "compact lines wrapped into boxed or captioned sub-blocks"
        - "class-form panel shows ghost or placeholder rows"
        - "captions not small caps or missing letter spacing"
    split-fidelity:
      weight: 0.2
      description: The split panel shows escaped monospace source on the left, the rendered card on the right, one shared pill row with SIDE BY SIDE active.
      fail_signals:
        - "code syntax highlighting colours on the source half"
        - "pill row missing or wrong active pill"
        - "rendered half showing raw markup"
    theme-match:
      weight: 0.15
      description: Dark minimal-tech surfaces, hairline borders, mono/sans split, AA-legible text everywhere.
      fail_signals:
        - "light background anywhere"
        - "neon glow or gradient gloss"
        - "text failing contrast"
